<h2>Where should the filters go on the account activity page?</h2>
<p class="subtitle">Wireframes only: layout, not final styling. All three sit inside the existing panel, above the table, and include a result count that screen readers announce.</p>

<div class="options">
  <div class="option" data-choice="a" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">A</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Filter bar, always visible</h3>
      <p>Labeled fields in a row above the table. Everything is on screen, nothing hidden. Wraps to a stack on narrow screens.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-end">
            <div><div class="label">Event</div><input class="mock-input" value="Sign-in failed" readonly></div>
            <div><div class="label">Date range</div><input class="mock-input" value="Last 7 days" readonly></div>
            <div><div class="label">Search</div><input class="mock-input" placeholder="Device, location, details" readonly></div>
            <button class="mock-button">Clear filters</button>
          </div>
          <p class="subtitle" style="margin-top:8px">Showing 6 of 48 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table: When, Event, Device, Location, IP, Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="option" data-choice="b" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">B</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>"Filters" button with a popover, plus tags</h3>
      <p>One button opens a panel with the fields. Applied filters show as removable tags. Compact, but the options are one click away and less discoverable.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center">
            <button class="mock-button">Filters (2)</button>
            <span class="placeholder" style="padding:4px 8px">Event: Sign-in failed  x</span>
            <span class="placeholder" style="padding:4px 8px">Last 7 days  x</span>
          </div>
          <p class="subtitle" style="margin-top:8px">Showing 6 of 48 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table: When, Event, Device, Location, IP, Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="option" data-choice="c" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">C</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Event type select plus a "Failed sign-ins" shortcut</h3>
      <p>Smallest version. One Event select and a quick button for the case every support ticket was about. No search or dates.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-end">
            <div><div class="label">Event</div><input class="mock-input" value="All events" readonly></div>
            <button class="mock-button">Show failed sign-ins</button>
          </div>
          <p class="subtitle" style="margin-top:8px">Showing 48 of 48 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table: When, Event, Device, Location, IP, Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
